86492037 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492037 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "92a47338-e5c2-507b-a67f-16316e526b27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492037 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+4|\\begin{aligned}2 & -\\lambda  \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+6{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda -12)-2(-2-2\\lambda )+4(4+4\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+6{\\lambda }^{2}+15\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-6{\\lambda }^{2}-15\\lambda -8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of $8:$ \n\n$$\n\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 4,\\pm 8\n$$\n\n- Let's pick $x=1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}-6(1)^{2}-15(1)-8 & =-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =1$ is not a root of the equation.\n\n- Let's pick $x=-1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{3}-6(-1)^{2}-15(-1)-8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =-1$ is a root of the equation.\n\nSo, we can factor $(\\lambda +1)$ out of ${\\lambda }^{3}-6{\\lambda }^{2}-15\\lambda -8$ using synthetic division:\n\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $-6$ | $-15$ | $-8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $↓$ | $-1$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-7$ | $-8$ | $0$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +1)({\\lambda }^{2}-7\\lambda -8) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -8) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=8.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492076 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186492106 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492076 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "09549905-c795-54bf-8c12-03fa23a953b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492076 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186492037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492085 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186492087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492085 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2d974ac8-4b52-5e20-b579-6e1ce93781a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492085 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492087 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186492076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492087 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "340f24d2-fb9b-5c2f-b6ce-923f20f3fce5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492087 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492099 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "95cae298-e2af-5367-a5a3-02954c8d6de6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492099 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186272102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492106 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186492099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492106 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c5e318ec-24f1-53a2-b4da-1e201af09eaa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492106 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186366518 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
